<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
  com.scannerproject.airband-ui (SB7.6)

  The web dashboard (ui/app.py, stdlib http.server on 0.0.0.0:5050) — status,
  hit log, squelch/gain controls, sitrep, and (once Will wires up SDRTrunk
  profiles) the digital view. Runs under /opt/scannerproject/venv, NOT
  radioconda — ui/chirp_client.py and ui/chirp_adapter.py are stdlib-only by
  design so the UI never needs a gnuradio import to talk to the chirp
  daemons over UDP.

  Unlike the chirp/tuner-broker plists, this one does NOT hardcode its
  environment. ui/config.py reads ~140 os.getenv() calls (every path, unit
  name, and port the UI needs), and scannerproject.env's own header comment
  says exactly this file is meant to be sourced by "every scannerproject
  process (UI, op25 bridge, decoders)". Duplicating that many vars into the
  plist would create a second copy that silently drifts from the real one —
  precisely the stale-config bug class this project keeps finding elsewhere
  (chirp/config/airband.json, the fleet policy). So ProgramArguments is a
  small zsh wrapper that sources the env file, then execs the UI — matching
  exactly how it was launched by hand for testing during 2026-07-06 bring-up.

  Runs from /opt/scannerproject/app (the rsync deploy copy), NOT the
  ~/Documents git checkout, for the same TCC reason as every other SB7
  service: a headless launchd process touching ~/Documents hangs on the
  consent check with no UI to answer it (macos-launchagent-tcc memory
  finding, 2026-07-05).

  Install (LaunchAgent, user session):
    cp etc/mac/launchd/com.scannerproject.airband-ui.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.scannerproject.airband-ui.plist
  Logs: /opt/scannerproject/log/airband-ui.log
  URL:  http://<m1-tailscale-ip>:5050/sb5
-->
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.scannerproject.airband-ui</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/zsh</string>
        <string>-c</string>
        <string>set -a; source /opt/scannerproject/etc/scannerproject.env; set +a; exec /opt/scannerproject/venv/bin/python ui/airband_ui.py</string>
    </array>

    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/opt/scannerproject/app</string>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>
    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <true/>
    <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
    <integer>10</integer>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/opt/scannerproject/log/airband-ui.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/opt/scannerproject/log/airband-ui.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
